  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Unlocking the Zhangping Shui Xian tea industry#s potential with digital skills upgrading and women empowerment</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The present project concept to upgrade tea industry supporting women&apos;s empowerment in Zhangping, Longyan City, Fujian Province of China, was developed following the respective request received from Ms. Lin Yan, the President of the Women&apos;s Federation of Longyan City, in an official letter addressed to Mr. Ciyong Zou, Deputy to the Director General and TCS Managing Director.  The present concept note was elaborated taking into account national development priorities and specific needs of the Zhangping Shui Xian tea industry, which is faced with multiple challenges that include supply chain inefficiencies, limited product value and market competitiveness, and gaps in effective marketing and branding strategies. Additionally, there&apos;s a missed opportunity in harnessing the synergies between the tea sector and tourism, positioning the Zhangping, Longyan City, Fujian Province as an attractive destination. Moreover, the industry is confronted with a notable digital skills gap, especially among women, highlighting both a technological lag and existing gender disparities. These hurdles emphasize the pressing need for modern digital upgrading based on the gender mainstreaming considerations, unlocking inclusivity opportunities offered by the digital age. The proposed project provides a concrete step-by-step intervention</narrative>
  </description>
